{% extends "_base.j2" %}
{% block body %}
Write the "Experiments" section of a paper in {{ language }}.

Topic: {{ topic }}
Section name: {{ section.name }}
Target words: about {{ words_target }}.

Methods (from outline): {{ section.brief }}

Measured metrics (computed by our sandbox):
{% for k, v in metrics.items() %}
- {{ k }}: {{ "%.4f"|format(v) }}
{% endfor %}
{% if extra %}
Auxiliary outputs:
{% for k, v in extra.items() %}
- {{ k }}: {{ v }}
{% endfor %}
{% endif %}

Style requirements
- Plain prose, no markdown headings, no bullet lists.
- Discuss setup, then results, then a brief analysis.
- Cite the metrics by their actual numeric values; do NOT invent
  additional numbers.
- Do NOT mention that the experiments were generated by AI or run in
  a sandbox.
{% endblock %}
